    value: 10.5281/zenodo.14524954
repository-code: 'https://geologica.gov.pk/volume10/'
url: >-
  https://geologica.gov.pk/volume10/15/12/2024/a-systematic-approach-for-standardization-of-colours-and-codes-for-various-geological-formations-of-pakistan/2893/
abstract: >-
  Standardized colours and codes are essential for ensuring
  consistency in geological mapping. Currently, the
  Geological Survey of Pakistan lacks a unified theme for
  assigning colours and formation codes. This paper details
  the process and results of an initiative aimed at
  standardizing these codes and colours. We utilised the
  USGS colour scheme as a foundation to develop a tailored
  colour chart for the Geological Survey of Pakistan. It was
  very challenging to allocate a unique colour to each
  formation while ensuring that these colours are easily
  distinguishable across different maps. Our findings
  indicate that the adoption of these standardized codes and
  colours significantly improves the clarity of geological
  maps, enhances understanding among researchers, and
  fosters better collaboration among stakeholders. This
  standardized scheme provides a uniform reference system,
  thereby increasing the usability of geological maps and
  supporting more accurate and efficient geological analysis
  and communication.
keywords:
  - Pakistan
  - stratigraphy
  - colour and codes
